## Project Architecture

The project uses a monolithic NestJS service (no NestJS modules) and is organized into strict layers:

src/
-application/                 # APPLICATION LAYER
--rest/
---[controller-name]/         # NestJS controllers
----dto/                      # Incoming/outgoing DTOs (must not cross into domain)
--amqp/
---[subcriber-name]/          # Message subscribers (RabbitMQ, etc.)
----dto/                      # Incoming/outgoing DTOs (must not cross into domain)    
domain/                       # DOMAIN LAYER
-models/                      # Domain entities + MikroORM annotations
-services/                    
--[service-name]/             # Domain services (business logic)
-infrastructure/              # INFRASTRUCTURE LAYER
--[provider-name]/            # External API clients, adapters, utilities
-migrations/                  # MikroORM migrations (auto-generated)

---

## Core Architectural Rules

### Layer Boundaries (Strict)
- **DTOs must never leak into the domain layer.**
  - Map DTOs to domain objects before calling domain services.
- **Controllers and subscribers must never contain business logic.**
  - They only validate, map, and call the domain.
- **Application layer must NOT depend on infrastructure.**
  - Only domain services can use infrastructure.
- **Domain services must not expose infrastructure-specific types.**
- **Do not create or use NestJS modules.**  
  This is a monolithic service by design.

---

## Responsibilities per Layer

### Application Layer (`application/`)
- Exposes the service externally (REST or AMQP).
- Contains DTOs, controllers, and subscribers.
- Responsibilities:
  - Validate input.
  - Map data to domain objects.
  - Call domain services.
  - Return response data.
- Forbidden:
  - Business logic.
  - Direct calls to infrastructure.
  - Returning domain entities directly (use DTOs for input/output).

### Domain Layer (`domain/`)
- Contains the full business logic.
- Responsibilities:
  - Domain models with MikroORM annotations.
  - Domain services with pure business logic.
- Rules:
  - Domain services may depend on infrastructure services via DI.
  - Domain entities represent real business concepts.
  - No DTOs, no NestJS request/response objects.

### Infrastructure Layer (`infrastructure/`)
- Contains adapters to external systems and technical concerns.
- Responsibilities:
  - API clients.
  - Authentication handling with external third parties.
  - Data mapping from external sources.
- Rules:
  - Must not be called directly from application.
  - Should expose clean methods for domain consumption.
  - Hide external API complexity from the rest of the system.

### Migrations (`migrations/`)
- Auto-generated by MikroORM.
- Should not contain manual logic.

---

## Additional AI Generation Rules

### Controller/Subscriber Generation
- Keep controllers minimal.
- Do not include any business logic.
- Always call a domain service, never infrastructure.

### Domain Service Generation
- Must operate only on domain models.
- Must contain all business rules.
- Should accept plain data objects or domain entities.
- No DTOs or technical types.

### Infrastructure Service Generation
- Encapsulate all external API details.
- Expose simple, domain-friendly methods.
- Do not leak infrastructure types into domain.

---

## Examples

### ✔️ Correct Call Flow
application → domain → infrastructure

### ❌ Incorrect Call Flow
application → infrastructure  
(application bypassing business logic)